meta {
  name: 04 Read one payment
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  One payment. `{{paymentId}}` is captured for you by `02 Create payment`.

  ## The check that matters

  ANOTHER CENTER'S PAYMENT ANSWERS 404, NEVER 403.

  To see it: register a second center, log in as it, and request the first
  center's `paymentId`. You get 404 PAYMENT_NOT_FOUND.

  403 would mean "this exists but is not yours", which is itself an answer —
  it lets someone confirm an id by probing. 404 says nothing either way. The
  student routes follow the same rule, deliberately.

  ## Other checks

  - a made-up id -> 404, identical response. Indistinguishable from the case
    above, which is the point.
  - no Authorization header -> 401.
  - a STUDENT access token -> 401. The center verifier refuses student tokens.

  ## What you are looking at

  `status` is PENDING and will stay PENDING for the whole of this phase.
  `unitPriceXaf` and `amountXaf` are snapshots taken when the payment was
  created, not a live lookup — if the center's contracted price changes next
  year, this record still says what was agreed today.
}
